# Project Rules

Next.js App Router project deployed on Coolify with direct Postgres.

## Stack

- Next.js / React / TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Direct Postgres through `postgres`
- Resend for email
- AI generation through configured provider APIs
- Coolify deployment from GitHub `main`

## Conventions

- Keep data access server-side.
- Use `DATABASE_URL` in production when available; `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_NAME`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD` are supported as fallback.
- Do not expose secrets to client components.
- Prefer small server helpers under `lib/` and API validation with Zod.
- Keep admin routes protected by signed `admin_session` checks.
- Verify with `npm test`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` before pushing.

## Database

- Schema lives under `db/migrations/`.
- Run migrations against the Coolify Postgres database before deploying schema-dependent features.
- Public pages should degrade gracefully when local database env vars are absent.
